1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Dubai has almost no oil left.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:05,740
Less than 1% of its economy runs on it.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:10,140
So how does a desert city pull in 30 million tourists a year

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:12,939
and host more billionaires than most countries?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:16,320
It starts with zero income tax.

6
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:21,039
For individuals and until recently, most businesses too.

7
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:25,239
That single policy turned Dubai into a magnet

8
00:00:25,239 --> 00:00:26,359
for global wealth.

9
00:00:27,170 --> 00:00:30,500
Add over 30 free trade zones where foreign companies

10
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:34,939
can own 100% of their business, pay no corporate tax,

11
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:36,820
and move profits freely,

12
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:40,640
and you've built the easiest place on earth to park money.

13
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:42,659
Then there's the port.

14
00:00:43,740 --> 00:00:46,219
Jebel Ali is the busiest in the Middle East,

15
00:00:46,619 --> 00:00:49,539
moving cargo between Asia, Europe, and Africa.

16
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:53,659
Emirates and Dubai International Airport turn the city

17
00:00:53,659 --> 00:00:55,500
into the world's connecting hub.

18
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:59,259
80% of the planet is under eight hours away.

19
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,899
Real estate did the rest.

20
00:01:02,859 --> 00:01:07,260
The Burj Khalifa, Palm Jumeirah, entire artificial islands

21
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:11,359
built to attract the ultra-rich, then sold to them,

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,260
then taxed through fees, not income.

23
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,459
Oil built the roads.

24
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:20,099
Everything after that is what actually pays the bills.
